PUBLIC RESPONSE: {Colleagues 1, 5, 9, 13, and 14 continue to present the cleanest alignment with the StarCraft II-era nomenclature that now dominates the thread. The Dominion–Zerg resurgence that receives the “Second Great War” label begins with the late-2504 Wings of Liberty events and reaches its decisive close on Char in Heart of the Swarm during 2505. That core interval is only twelve to eighteen months of sustained large-scale operations once the earlier Brood War cleanup and the later Legacy of the Void epilogue are kept distinct, exactly as the Chronicle and in-universe summaries treat them.  

The documented late-2503 brood-mother skirmishes and the immediate post-Char political consolidation add only the partial-year buffers that the same inclusive ceiling convention already applied to the Brood War itself. Those flanking months push the total elapsed span just over one calendar year and therefore round cleanly to two under the manuals’ standard practice. Extending the count through 2506–2507 would require folding the Aiur End War operations into the same conflict label—an inclusion the official chronologies explicitly avoid.  

The broader 2504–2507 bracket therefore collapses once the separate End War arc is set aside. The narrower 2504–2505 window with its flanking buffers remains the reading that best matches both the game dates and the lore summaries without importing events already assigned to other campaigns.}

